WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.992
The elderly Taoist Qiu Chuji received Genghis Khan's invitation.

00:00:05.342 --> 00:00:08.030
The old Taoist nodded calmly.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:13.108
Qiu Chuji, with his disciples, began the long journey west.

00:00:13.458 --> 00:00:17.586
All along the road there was wind-blown sand and hardship upon hardship.

00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:22.880
In the year 1222, the two finally met in Central Asia.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.254
The two old men respected each other.

00:00:26.604 --> 00:00:31.692
Qiu Chuji spoke of the way of nurturing life, and also of the principles of governing a state.

00:00:32.042 --> 00:00:35.858
Inside the great tent, the mood was warm and solemn.

00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:41.368
The old Taoist urged Genghis Khan to reduce killing and cherish life.

00:00:41.718 --> 00:00:43.998
Genghis Khan listened earnestly.

00:00:44.348 --> 00:00:50.084
The disciples wrote this journey down as the 'Travels of the Perfected Changchun to the West'.

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:54.082
By lamplight, the disciple wrote with concentration.

